\paragraph{Features learned by FB.}
\Cref{fig:fb-features} shows the features of a trained FB critic with two features, where they can be drawn in the plane.
FB gives the rewarded states $3,4$ exactly the same features as the unrewarded states $5,6$ (to numerical precision, in all ten runs).
The average feature vector of the future after $a_+$ therefore equals that after $a_-$, which is the condition of \cref{lem:bottleneck-loss}, and FB predicts the same future and the same value ($0.62$) for both actions.

